{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6be48c6629b9afb8","name":"R4-Series Astromech Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-6be48c6629b9afb8","title":"R4-Series Astromech Droid","revision":19001,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:07:05Z","sha256":"57b55090694d4f3b0bd29a60d1afe8118a68bc880be9666ed625d9a236fa9f67","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19001","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=R4-Series%20Astromech%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6be48c6629b9afb8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["R3-Series Astromech Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/R3-Series_Astromech_Droid","referenceId":"reference:d8d8bbfc862aca99"},", the R4-Series was designed after the success of its predecessor, the R2-Series. However, the R4-Series was created to appeal to lower-income users who did not own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," but might have ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeders","referenceId":"reference:be93ac2e4867f0ca"}," or other devices that would break down regularly. The R4 was made to be durable but inexpensive, causing it to be extremely popular with residents of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim Territories"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim_Territories?action=edit&redlink=1"},". As a result, a large number of these Droids continue to operate for many years after their construction.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The R4 Droid is quite versatile and able to perform many functions within the scope of its programming. Although ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," work was not originally conceived for the R4, high demand from various organizations prompted the creation of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," variant with the recognizable curved dome from the R2-Series instead of the truncated cone found on the standard model. IA's review of R4-P17's rebuilt body and integration into Obi-Wan Kenobi's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Delta-7 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Aethersprite"]}," Interceptor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Delta-7_Aethersprite_Interceptor","referenceId":"reference:6406918844c52156"}," by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Anakin Skywalker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker","referenceId":"reference:e7c68f75d23b428e"}," inspired the cosmetic changes for the R4's designed strictly for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," work.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Many of the features available through previous models, such as video displays and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fire Extinguishers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fire_Extinguishers"},", were not made available in the R4 to cut down on production costs. As a result, the R4 has more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Internal Storage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Internal_Storage"}," than normal for a Droid of its size.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["R4-Series Astromech Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["R4-Series Astromech Droid Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Much like the R3-Series, the R4 can be found virtually everywhere in its intended market, most often on Outer Rim worlds. Since the personality programmed into the R4 was more successful than expected, being more friendly and loyal than even the R2, most owners come to treat their Droid as more of a pet or companion rather than a servant. As a result, the Droid's memory is typically not wiped unless it changes owners- and not always even then. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though the low-income user in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"}," was the original sales target, other people throughout the galaxy have seen the merits of owning a R4 Droid. Some owners like the appeal of the Droid's pleasant personality and used it in such capacities as assisting salespeople in retail stores as far coreward as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," and serving drinks in some of Ord Mantell's lower-end casinos. R4s have worked aboard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," as well, such as the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Tantive IV"]},", operating alongside R2 units performing jobs more fitting for an Astromech Droid. In service to the Empire, a few R4s equipped with magnetic fault sensors were used to detect flaws and weak spots in the first Death Star's atmosphere containment fields. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Some R4 Droids have turned up in the hands of the Rebellion, serving in a multitude of ways from computer assistants to messengers and from repair assistants to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," astrogators. The Rebellion appreciated the model's low cost and extensive knowledge of general-purpose ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", earning the Droids a place on many Alliance bases and in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mon Calamari"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mon_Calamari","referenceId":"reference:5b784aed2214627b"}," hangar bays.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although the R4 line was not originally intended to see combat, many units witnessed and participated in more battles than even the R3, especially the R4 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," variant, and thus the R4 is second only to the R2 as far as flight experience is concerned. R4s tend to be a little braver than other Droids when it comes to a fight. A few have even been eager to jump into the fray to help their masters, only to find themselves overwhelmed and quickly dispatched. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["R4-Series Astromech Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defen